# $version() -> Character
# The hand-kept version of Executor.lbs. One number, raised by a person when
# the tool reaches a state worth naming. Nothing raises it automatically.
#
# It is NOT the build number. The build lives in the library's own $userinfo,
# tagged EXEC-BUILD=, and Startup_Task.$bumpBuild raises it by one for every
# library a run actually changed -- worked out from mDiff in
# ExecutorConsole.$runInVessel, which is the only place that knows.
#
# So: $version says which tool this is, EXEC-BUILD says how many runs have
# changed it. Read the build with
#     Calculate name as $root.$libs.Executor.$userinfo
# or see it in the Property Manager, where it is plain text.
#
# Semantic versioning (semver.org): MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, a pre-release suffix while in beta.
# Raise it by hand on a release and record the change in _Changelog.
Quit method '1.0.0'